<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Julian Reese on a Two-Way Contract?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Reese is paid <strong>$679k</strong> because he is on a two-way contract, and the two-way rate is fixed by the collective agreement for everyone on one.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went undrafted in 2025 and began on an Exhibit 10 deal with Toronto, playing for Raptors 905.</li>
<li>Washington signed him to a two-way deal in February 2026, and he averaged 11.8 points and 10.5 rebounds in 13 games.</li>
<li>He was traded and waived in August before New Orleans signed him.</li>
<li>Only <strong>$91k</strong> of the contract is protected.</li>
<li>He is a 6-9 forward.</li>
</ul>
<p>New Orleans is the fourth NBA club he has been with in a year.</p>

